theory.intro:
The **magnitude** of a vector is its length, written $|\underset{\sim}{a}|$. Pythagoras' theorem on the components gives $|\underset{\sim}{a}|=\sqrt{x^{2}+y^{2}}$. A length is never negative.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=1.2]
\usetikzlibrary{arrows.meta,calc}
\coordinate (O) at (0,0);
\coordinate (P) at (4,3);
\coordinate (Q) at (4,0);
\draw[dashed] (O)--(Q) node[midway,below]{$x$};
\draw[dashed] (Q)--(P) node[midway,right]{$y$};
\draw[-{Stealth},thick] (O)--(P) node[midway,above left]{$|\underset{\sim}{a}|$};
\coordinate (r1) at ($(Q)!0.35cm!(O)$);
\coordinate (r2) at ($(Q)!0.35cm!(P)$);
\draw (r1)--($(r1)+(r2)-(Q)$)--(r2);
\node[above right] at (P) {$\underset{\sim}{a}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
The displacement is $\underset{\sim}{d}=8\underset{\sim}{i}+5\underset{\sim}{j}$ km.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=5mm,y=5mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\definecolor{vectorBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}
\draw[->,draw=black,thick] (0,0)--(8,0);
\draw[->,draw=black,thick] (8,0)--(8,5);
\draw[->,draw=vectorBlue,thick] (0,0)--(8,5);
\draw[draw=black] (7.6,0)--(7.6,0.4)--(8,0.4);
\path (4,0) node[below] {$8\text{ km east}$};
\path (8,2.5) node[right] {$5\text{ km north}$};
\path (3.5,2.7) node[above left] {$\underset{\sim}{d}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

$\begin{aligned}|\underset{\sim}{d}|&=\sqrt{8^2+5^2}\\&=\sqrt{89}\\&\approx9.43\end{aligned}$

The final displacement has magnitude $9.43$ km.

development.solution_text:
$\underset{\sim}{a}+\underset{\sim}{b}=\begin{pmatrix}4+(-1)\\1+5\end{pmatrix}$
$=\begin{pmatrix}3\\6\end{pmatrix}$
$|\underset{\sim}{a}+\underset{\sim}{b}|=\sqrt{3^{2}+6^{2}}$
$=\sqrt{9+36}$
$=\sqrt{45}$
$=3\sqrt{5}$
